      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To investigate the relationship of microRNA 616 (has-miR-616) single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) and its target gene paraoxonase 1 (PON 1) with the prognosis of patients with premature coronary artery disease (pCAD)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "266 pCAD cases in the case group and 300 cases in the control group were collected. Using the polymorphism method of polymerase chain reaction and restriction fragment length, the has-miR-616 rs3735590 genotypes of target gene PON 1 were detected."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "In the changes of rs3735590 C/T SNPs, compared with CC genotypes, the risk of coronary heart disease of the individuals carrying CT and TT genotypes were reduced by 42% and 31%, respectively (p < 0.05). The risk of developing coronary heart disease in individuals carrying CT and TT genotypes were reduced significantly in the population with levels of total cholesterol, high-density lipoprotein cholesterol, and low-density lipoprotein cholesterol."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Target gene PON 1 of hsa-miRNA-616 rs3735590C-T SNPs is associated with the reduced incidence risk of pCAD, and carrying C alleles is an independent risk factor for pCAD."
        }
      ]},
